INT. ABANDONED HOTEL POOL - DAWN

A drained lap pool under a skylight patched with plywood. Peeling blue tiles. A diving board with one rusted bolt. Pale light falls in stripes across the floor of the deep end.

HENRIK SOLBERG, sixties, in a long wool coat, sits on a plastic chair at the shallow end with a stopwatch hanging from his neck. He is a retired coach with a patient, ruined face. At the edge of the deep end, ASHA NDLOVU-REYES, twenty, in a tracksuit, stretches her shoulders and rolls her neck. She has not looked at him since she arrived.

He clears his throat. She does not turn.

She steps onto the diving board. It flexes and groans beneath her bare feet. She bounces once, testing, and the whole structure sings, and he half rises from the chair.

HENRIK
Asha.

ASHA
It's fine.

HENRIK
The board is not fine.

ASHA
It has held before.

He sits back down, slowly. The stopwatch swings against his chest. She bounces again, higher, and the bolt shrieks in its socket, and still she does not stop.

HENRIK
The pool is empty.

ASHA
I know.

HENRIK
I only mention it.

She laughs, a short surprised sound that echoes off the tiles. She lowers herself to the end of the board and sits there, legs dangling above eleven feet of nothing.

ASHA
Do you remember the last time you timed me?

HENRIK
Sydney.

ASHA
You said I was a second slow.

HENRIK
You were a second slow.

ASHA
I was a tenth slow. I looked it up.

He lifts the stopwatch. Studies it. Thumbs the button. It clicks.

HENRIK
Then it was a tenth.

She stands again. Walks to the very edge. Spreads her arms and looks up at the skylight, where the plywood has split to let in one thin blade of gold.

ASHA
Start the watch.

HENRIK
For what?

ASHA
Just start it.

He starts it. She bends her knees. Holds. And then, softly, to nobody, she dives, a clean arc, arms together, into the long empty blue, and at the last instant her fingertips brush the floor and she rolls and comes up laughing, breathless, filthy, alive.

He stops the watch. Looks at it. Does not say the number.
